2. Proposed architecture

The discussion points toward roughly three layers.

A. Market / franchise overview

A small number of common introductory pages giving management context before diving into individual clients.

B. One page per originator/client

A consistent template, initially tested on one or two clients, then replicated.

Names specifically mentioned included approximately:

* Together
* Pepper
* Enra
* Foundation
* LendInvest
* Lendco/Fabrus

The logic was to show more than just the three current/core clients because otherwise the exercise artificially forces a choice among a tiny universe. Management should see the relevant UK specialist mortgage market, including both existing and potential clients.

C. Portfolio / strategic ask

Potential concluding pages showing:

* current and desired balance-sheet allocation;
* returns and economics;
* maturity/run-off;
* potential client mix;
* upside from public distribution and other fee opportunities;
* possibly what business has been lost/declined because of constraints.

There was some debate about whether this explicit “ask” belongs in the first version or should be kept “in the back pocket.”

