9. Economics / returns

Management should see clean economics.

Metrics specifically mentioned included:

* revenues;
* facility returns over the last 12 months;
* ROE;
* SVA;
* utilisation;
* balance-sheet usage;
* potentially historical improvement in those metrics.

The discussion emphasised that ROE is relevant but should not be the only decision criterion.

A high-return client may still differ materially in:

* scale;
* stability;
* strategic relevance;
* distribution potential;
* product breadth;
* franchise value.

Likewise, lower-return prime distribution mandates may still be attractive because they consume no balance sheet and generate pure fees.

