10. Actual economics versus “steady-state” economics

This was a particularly useful concept discussed.

The deck should distinguish:

Reported/actual economics

What was actually earned.

Economics forgone because of constraints or deliberate decisions

Examples:

* waived exit fees;
* mandates skipped because of MFS;
* deals where the bank did not pitch;
* rejected commitment increases;
* accordions not funded;
* public roles/JLM opportunities foregone.

Then show something like:

Actual: £X
+ identifiable forgone/waived economics: £Y
Indicative steady-state economics: £X+Y

The transcript explicitly stressed wanting “clean numbers, actuals”, followed by a transparent bridge showing what had been waived or forgone.

Not to pretend forgone revenues were earned, but to demonstrate the underlying franchise opportunity.

