11. Lost / declined business

This should feature somewhere in the deck.

Two possibilities discussed:

* dedicated slide near the back; or
* client-level footnote/callout.

Include relevant examples such as:

* public transactions where the bank did not participate;
* JLM opportunities not pursued;
* commitment increases declined;
* accordion increases refused;
* deals consciously skipped because of MFS/balance-sheet restrictions.

An important nuance:

Not every commitment increase would formally be a “Salesforce lost opportunity,” but it can still be relevant in the strategic deck because it demonstrates latent demand from existing clients.

The objective is to show:

“The business did not disappear because clients stopped offering us opportunities; some opportunities were deliberately constrained or declined.”

