12. Client stability / quality as a strategic dimension

The deck should not reduce decision-making to pure return.

Factors mentioned included:

* operating history;
* resilience through cycles;
* scale;
* stability of origination;
* willingness to step away when markets become irrational;
* management quality;
* product diversification;
* reputation;
* sponsor backing;
* strategic behaviour.

For example, the conversation contrasted stable operators that reduce origination when pricing becomes uneconomic with lenders chasing volume.

This should feed into the ultimate client-selection framework.

