18. Presentation philosophy

Several very clear presentation principles emerged.

Keep slides light

Explicit preference:

“I prefer lighter and more graphs, less words.”

Management may only spend a few minutes absorbing the information.

Use scale visually

Graphs should make instantly visible:

* client A is 3x client B;
* client represents X% of issuance;
* bank is top 3 out of 12;
* current exposure versus client funding requirement;
* market share of core clients.

Treat management as knowledgeable bankers but not sector experts

The team “knows this inside out”; management does not.

The deck therefore needs enough context to prevent incorrect conclusions without turning into a 100-page sector primer.

Do not overcomplicate version one

The explicit philosophy was roughly:

Stage 1: establish market, clients, franchise, economics and strategic choices.

More ambitious product expansion can come later.

