20. How the deck should be built

The process discussed was pragmatic.

First collect everything into one place

Gather:

* previous MFG decks;
* pre/post-MFS strategy decks;
* prior growth decks;
* banking slides;
* M&A materials;
* client presentations;
* prior first-lien/second-lien work;
* professional-perfection / strategy material;
* issuance charts;
* existing tombstones;
* pitch materials for Pepper/Enra;
* external data.

The instruction was essentially:

“Dump all the resources in one folder.”

Then review collectively for useful data and visual ideas.

Prototype the template

Create one or two client pages first.

Agree:

* what information is essential;
* which charts work;
* whether one or two pages per client are necessary.

Then replicate.

Do not wait for a perfect template before data collection begins.

Parallelise work

People can start populating version 1 while the template evolves.

If the team later decides:

“Add this, add this,”

they update to version 2.

The speaker explicitly accepted that the first version would not be perfect and some data would initially be missing.

